# The hosts that run these are Linux, and the laptop that edits them is not.
# A systemd unit with CRLF endings takes the carriage return as part of the
# value, so ExecStart tries to run a binary whose name ends in \r. Pinning the
# ending here means it cannot depend on whose machine wrote the file.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
